Both functions below compute the same sum over a 4096×4096 `Float64Array` stored row by row. One is several times slower. Which one, and why? 

```js
function a(g, N) { let s = 0; for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) for (let j = 0; j < N; j++) s += g[i * N + j]; return s; }
function b(g, N) { let s = 0; for (let j = 0; j < N; j++) for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) s += g[i * N + j]; return s; }
```
